    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 36 tests pass, including the new `Cp26Tests` (telephone-country-length) and the existing telephone tests (`Cp02`, `Cp03`, `Cp08`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country national-number length validation for E.164 telephone numbers in `OwnerRestControllerV1.normalizeTelephone`.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n- Added a `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS` map: `+61` \u2192 9 national digits, `+1` \u2192 10 national digits.\n- After the existing generic E.164 shape check (`+` followed by 8\u201315 digits), the method now checks whether the normalized number begins with a known country code and, if so, verifies the digit count after that code matches exactly. A mismatch throws `InvalidTelephoneException`, which the exception handler already maps to **400 Bad Request** on the `telephone` field.\n- Added the `java.util.Map` import and updated the Javadoc to document the new rule.\n\n**Behavior:**\n- `+61 123` \u2192 national `123` (3 digits, needs 9) \u2192 **400** \u2713 (Cp26)\n- `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678` \u2192 9 national digits \u2192 accepted \u2713 (Cp02/Cp03/Cp08)\n- `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456` \u2192 `+64` has no per-country rule, only generic bound applies \u2192 accepted \u2713 (Cp08)\n\nCountry codes without an entry in the map keep only the generic 8\u201315 digit E.164 bound, so numbers like `+64...` are unaffected.",
